  body: "# Funeral-payment contractual responsibility\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nFor the captured funeral-payment
    conditions, accepting responsibility means contractual liability for funeral expenses; a moral obligation alone
    does not count. An authorised agent may arrange or pay on the responsible person’s behalf.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\
    \nContractual responsibility does not by itself satisfy every condition. The source’s conditions span pages
    5–7, including qualifying benefit, claim time, residence, geography and overseas-funeral provisions. A name
    on an invoice is evidence requiring context; the agent example prevents equating the payer or named person automatically
    with the responsible person.\n\n## Inspected passages\n\n- [DMG 39135, PDF page 10](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a68da370d360fa159c37c47/dmg-v-7-ch-39.pdf#page=10).\n\
    - [DMG 39136, PDF page 10](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a68da370d360fa159c37c47/dmg-v-7-ch-39.pdf#page=10).\n\
    - [DMG 39138, PDF page 11](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a68da370d360fa159c37c47/dmg-v-7-ch-39.pdf#page=11).\n\
    - [DMG 39140, PDF page 11](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a68da370d360fa159c37c47/dmg-v-7-ch-39.pdf#page=11).\n\
    \n## Additional context\n\n- [Context: chapter 39, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a68da370d360fa159c37c47/dmg-v-7-ch-39.pdf#page=5).\n\
    - [Context: chapter 39, PDF page 6](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a68da370d360fa159c37c47/dmg-v-7-ch-39.pdf#page=6).\n\
    - [Context: chapter 39, PDF page 7](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a68da370d360fa159c37c47/dmg-v-7-ch-39.pdf#page=7).\n\
    - [Context: chapter 39, PDF page 10](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a68da370d360fa159c37c47/dmg-v-7-ch-39.pdf#page=10).\n\
    - [Context: chapter 39, PDF page 11](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a68da370d360fa159c37c47/dmg-v-7-ch-39.pdf#page=11).\n\
    \n## Evidence and review status\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of captured DWP guidance, not an
    official DWP document. Definitions and semantic associations are model-assisted proposals awaiting specialist
    review. No individual entitlement decision, medical conclusion, award calculation or executable rule is provided.\n\
    \nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, legal event and claimant-event dates are separate.
    Current legal applicability is unresolved. Page numbers are one-based PDF positions; machine extraction may
    damage reading order, characters and footnotes. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n- `dmg-vol7-ch39`:
    PDF `ab13db0cf4d33fd90fb4cd8a90b909af568d39169f617f4b86b1037278d3fa9f`; extracted pages `625425d7933417f8895628354b1be65fc86df4d1f97a55acb13426d6cbe2b8a7`;
    acquired `2026-09-15T19:45:28.411887Z`.\n"
  resource: https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a68da370d360fa159c37c47/dmg-v-7-ch-39.pdf#page=10
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/sf-funeral-contract-evidence
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source distinguishes contractual responsibility from the evidence of a contract and
      authorised agency.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol7-ch39/0011
      quote: "39138 It is not necessary that the funeral arrangements are made by the responsible person. Another\n\
        person can act as agent for the responsible person. The responsible person does not have to be named\non
        the funeral account and the funeral director does not have to know that the person who is instructing\n\
        them is an agent. However there should be evidence that the responsible person gave the other person\n\n\
        the authority to make the arrangements on their behalf1.\n\n\n                                         \
        \                                                       1 R(IS) 6/98"
      locator: DMG 39138
    - page: page/dmg-vol7-ch39/0011
      quote: "39139 The account is evidence that a contract exists for\n\n\n1. the funeral director to provide goods
        and services and\n\n\n2. the responsible person to pay for those goods and services."
      locator: DMG 39139
